    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a conservative outlook, as the scarcity of premium matchups leaves our roster tethered to the lower end of the efficiency scale. **Kyle Tucker** (47.99) remains our most viable asset in the outfield, though he faces a stiff challenge against Henderson. While **Kyle Tucker** typically anchor our production, his drop to the #8 spot in the order significantly dampens his ceiling, turning what is usually an elite start into a marginal one. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (41.53) occupies the UTIL slot, narrowly clearing our 40-point threshold. Despite an elite stolen base profile, the combination of Henderson\u2019s sub-3.20 xERA and **Andy Pages**' lower-tier position in the lineup keeps his output restricted, highlighting the difficulty of navigating today\u2019s matchups.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 32.31. While **Brayan Rocchio** has shown flashes of recent consistency, the combination of a high-efficiency outing from Rasmussen and a weak #9 spot in the lineup pushed him well below our required 40.0 floor. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** either sidelined by off-days or the IL, the depth of the Austin Waves is severely tested. We are effectively playing for preservation today, particularly as we monitor the volatility of our lower-order hitters like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who\u2014while not listed in today\u2019s primary starters\u2014remain under internal review should the lineup structure shift ahead of first pitch. No major weather hazards are flagged, but the quality of opposing arms suggests a quiet night for our primary offensive targets.",
